use flake

# `use flake` watches flake.nix and flake.lock, not the dev-shell modules under
# nix/dev or the repo paths the Vale style build copies in: the overlay under
# .config/vale/local and the two verb dictionaries under
# crates/mindtape/src/dicts. Watching them makes direnv re-evaluate this file
# after an edit, which repoints target/vale/styles at the new build. A cached
# nix evaluation can still serve the old style. `lint::vale-levels` fails on
# a stale link.
watch_file nix/dev nix/dev/*.nix
shopt -s globstar
watch_file .config/vale/local/**
watch_file crates/mindtape/src/dicts/*.txt
